      "symptom": {
        "basis": "DIRECT_OBSERVATION",
        "text": "After server and control authenticated readiness, the invoker joined with server entity ID 2 but both GET /v1/handshake readiness requests returned authenticated HTTP 409 REQUEST_REJECTED with UNKNOWN outcome and retry_allowed=false.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "invoker-handshake-rejections",
          "server-control-readiness",
          "server-player-joins"
        ]
      },
      "trigger_conditions": {
        "basis": "DIRECT_OBSERVATION",
        "text": "The observer freezes boundEntityId and installs StaffPacketTrace synchronously in LoggingIn. The inspected Forge handleLogin disassembly calls firePlayerLogin at bytecode 383 before packet playerId at 387 and LocalPlayer.setId at 401. A provisional ID unequal to the final server ID will violate current() later.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "observer-before",
          "listener-disassembly",
          "forge-hooks-disassembly",
          "patched-bytecode-identity"
        ]
      },
      "root_cause": {
        "basis": "DIRECT_OBSERVATION",
        "text": "Implementation lifecycle defect: binding the numeric entity ID and packet witness during LoggingIn can retain the provisional ID before handleLogin assigns the final ID. This code/disassembly finding is distinct from an exact causal reconstruction of the V5 live rejection; the live provisional IDs and exception message were not retained.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "observer-before",
          "listener-disassembly",
          "forge-hooks-disassembly",
          "invoker-handshake-rejections",
          "patched-bytecode-identity"
        ]
      },
      "repair": {
        "basis": "DIRECT_OBSERVATION",
        "text": "LoggingIn consumes the epoch and retains the original player, connection lifetime and channel object without freezing the provisional entity ID or exposing a receiver. A one-shot END client tick revalidates those identities and the selected UUID, then binds the final entity ID. Receiver startup verifies and initializes its session and owned directory before a checked callback installs the packet trace; only a successful callback permits receiver activation. Logout, clone, duplicate login, identity loss and startup failure permanently invalidate the pending lifetime, and later entity-ID changes remain rejected.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "observer-after",
          "receiver-owner-after",
          "lifecycle-tests-after"
        ]
      },
      "lesson": {
        "basis": "INFERENCE",
        "text": "Defer final numeric identity and packet-witness binding until a verified post-login boundary, retaining the original player/connection checks and fail-closed lifetime semantics. A first client readiness success does not establish correct identity binding for later clients.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "observer-before",
          "listener-disassembly",
          "server-control-readiness",
          "server-player-joins"
        ]
      },
      "causal_chain": [
        {
          "basis": "INFERENCE",
          "text": "Control joined with server ID 1 and invoker with ID 2; the provisional client IDs were not captured. Control success is consistent with a coincidental provisional/final match, but does not prove one.",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "server-player-joins",
            "server-control-readiness"
          ]
        },
        {
          "basis": "DIRECT_OBSERVATION",
